    },
    "The full reference for fields, quality checks, slot tables and semantics is the repository file {c}docs/GENERATOR_AUTHORING_RU.md{c_}; this page gives you the road, that one gives you the letter of the contract.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:289"
    },
    "The list of generators": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:303"
    },
    "The manifest declares checks on the content of columns — {c}not_null{c_}, {c}unique{c_}, {c}range{c_}, {c}regex{c_}, {c}enum{c_}, {c}known_values{c_} — and the platform evaluates them on every run: the freshness of a source, a change in the number of rows, a column that went away, new values against a lookup table. A finding carries its own id, so «the same problem» is recognised across runs and a decision already made («we know, it is meant to be like that») does not have to be made again.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:330"
    },
    "The move that ends the problem: do not bake colours into the chart — read them from CSS variables and redraw the chart on the event the platform sends when the theme changes.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:462"
    },
    "The owner of a report can re-colour it right in the browser — the {b}Colors{b_} tab on the report page. Everything that lives in CSS and in SVG attributes is re-coloured. Charts on {c}&lt;canvas&gt;{c_} are painted pixels and CSS does not reach them: the platform changes plain colour strings through the library's API, but gradients, colour functions and scales stay as they were.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:461"
    },
    "The path of the data: files → build → report → questions → control": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:33"
    },
    "The platform finds the {c}&lt;script id=\"bootstrap-snapshot\" type=\"application/json\"&gt;{c_} tag and replaces its content with fresh JSON on every render. Leave a placeholder in the file.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:424"
    },
    "The platform shows its honest limits itself: a file taken from the cache was never opened by the generator — so nobody knows anything about its columns.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:320"
    },
    "The platform's libraries sit on the same server as the report and need no login — this is neither an external request nor a CDN. One caveat: a file downloaded to the desktop and opened with a double click will not find that address, so keep the file-picker zone from point 4 either way.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:409"
    },
    "The platform's lookup tables": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:351"
    },
    "The report is in place — and a workbench appears around it": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:184"
    },
    "The report list in the workspace": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:97"
    },
    "The report lives in an isolated window with no access to the platform, so files arrive as messages. The platform embeds its half of the protocol itself — your job is to listen and answer.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:401"
    },
    "The report must rebuild itself": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:119"
    },
    "The same conversation is available inside the report itself — as a pane on the right, without covering the numbers.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:369"
    },
    "The same report every week on new files. You write a generator in Python, the platform runs it in the analyst's browser and publishes the result.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:120"
    },
    "The server hands a report over in a fraction of a millisecond — all the time the reader sees goes into transferring and parsing the HTML in their browser. So the only effective optimisation is to {b}reduce what the browser parses{b_}. A report heavier than 1.5 MB no longer shows a live preview in the list; heavier than 2 MB and the upload page warns you.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:445"
    },
    "The typical «giant» is a small amount of visualisation code plus megabytes of JSON inside the markup. The cure is separation: an empty snapshot in the HTML and the data as a separate slot file, which the platform delivers to the report itself while the browser caches and decompresses it on the fly.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:446"
    },
    "The upload page": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:174"
    },
    "The workspace is the list of reports you have access to, with folders, favourites and live previews. Everything else in the left menu is a tool around that list: upload, generators, sources, quality, lookup tables, questions.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:91"
    },
