    },
    "{b}A picture or a script next to the file is missing.{b_} Upload the missing file as a slot — relative links inside the report resolve to it, and the markup needs no rework.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:480"
    },
    "{b}A white screen.{b_} A library is linked to an external site. The report runs in an isolated window and cannot reach out — ask the model to embed the library's code in the file.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:477"
    },
    "{b}Determinism.{b_} The same inputs give byte-identical outputs: sort anything that comes out of the OS's sets and dictionaries, fix the column order, never bake the generation time into the data. The equivalence gate and an honest cache both stand on this.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:258"
    },
    "{b}No input or output{b_} outside out_dir, cache_dir and the paths you are handed. No network, no threads, no subprocesses — WebAssembly has none of them, and the same code must keep working in plain CPython, because that is where it is tested.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:259"
    },
    "{b}The file upload works locally but not on the platform.{b_} The report reads the file input directly instead of listening to the protocol. Take the exact-protocol prompt above.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:478"
    },
    "{b}The generator never sees folders.{b_} An analyst may connect up to eight of them; the engine hands over a flat union, so classify files strictly by name.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:261"
    },
    "{b}The report shows yesterday's data.{b_} Nearly always an old version in the browser cache: reload the page bypassing the cache, and in future publish the data as a slot — its address changes together with its content.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:479"
    },
    "{b}interactive{b_} — the markup carries {c}&lt;input type=\"file\"&gt;{c_}. The reader brings the data: they load their own extract and the report draws it. Right when everyone has their own folder.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:391"
    },
    "{b}progress(stage, done, total, msg){b_} crosses the worker boundary. Call it once per file and once per major phase, never inside a loop over rows.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:260"
    },
    "{b}snapshot{b_} — the markup carries {c}&lt;script id=\"bootstrap-snapshot\"&gt;{c_}. The data is shared and updated centrally: the platform injects fresh JSON on every open. This is also the kind generators publish.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:392"
    },
    "{b}static{b_} — no special tags, the data is baked in at creation time. For a snapshot on a date and for presentations that must not change after the fact.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:393"
    },
    "«Upload» in the left menu, then drop the file. The result of the analysis appears on the right: the kind of report and the number of data slots. The kind is decided by the markup — {c}&lt;input type=\"file\"&gt;{c_} makes the report interactive, the {c}bootstrap-snapshot{c_} tag makes it a snapshot, and without either it is static. The difference is in the reference at the bottom of this page.": {
      "ref": "templates/pages/docs.html:169"
